<h1>Running a group</h1>
<p>We've run individual tests and reviewed every parameter type in the
  <a class="text-accent" href="/tutorial/basic-configuration-parameters-group/">Basic Configuration Parameters
  group</a>. Now we'll configure the group as one run and execute all nine tests together.</p>

<h2 id="reloading-the-session">Reloading the session</h2>
<p>For this demonstration, we'll first reload the session so every test starts from its source defaults. Select
  the session node, then click <strong class="text-danger">Reload</strong>:</p>
{{ media.zoomableImage("/assets/images/screenshots/tutorial/running-a-group/reloading-session.png", "Reload action for reloading all reloadable suites and top-level groups in the current Orcraft session from source", "large") }}
<p>The Reload action reloads <strong>every</strong> reloadable suite and top-level group in the current session,
  not only the item currently selected. We can use it here because our session contains only one added item - the
  Tutorial suite. In a normal session containing several items, we usually wouldn't reload the entire session
  just to prepare one group for a run.</p>

<h2 id="selecting-the-group">Selecting the group</h2>
<p>In the Test Explorer, select the <strong>Basic Configuration Parameters</strong> group rather than one of its
  child tests. The Configuration tab switches to a multi-test view: the tests appear in a tree on the left, and
  selecting a test opens its configuration on the right.</p>
{{ media.zoomableImage("/assets/images/screenshots/tutorial/running-a-group/selecting-basic-config-params-group.png", "Basic Configuration Parameters group selected in the Orcraft Test Explorer, with the multi-test configuration table and Folder Parameter editor visible", "large") }}
<p>This is still one group run, but every test keeps its own fields, cases and planned values. Move through the
  test list to configure each one before starting the run. The table provides a quick overview of all test
  values, while the editor below it lets us configure the selected test.</p>
<p><strong>All action buttons at the bottom now apply to the entire group.</strong> For example,
  <strong class="text-accent">Update Plan</strong> saves the configuration of every child test, and
  <strong>Reset To Defaults</strong> resets every child test - not only the test currently selected in the editor.
  The same group-wide scope applies to <strong>Export for CI</strong> and <strong>Run</strong>. Selecting a child in
  the table only chooses which test's fields are shown for editing.</p>

<h2 id="configuring-the-tests">Configuring the tests</h2>
<p>Every child test must have valid values. Fields marked as required can't be left empty:</p>
<ul>
  <li>Set <strong>Maze Executable Folder</strong> for Folder, Boolean, Selector, File, File List, Numeric,
    Multi-Selector and String Parameter.</li>
  <li>Add at least one entry to <strong>Maze Executable Folders</strong> for Folder List Parameter.</li>
  <li>Select a saved maze file for <strong>Maze Save/Load File</strong> in File Parameter.</li>
  <li>Select one or more saved maze files for <strong>Maze Save/Load Files</strong> in File List Parameter.</li>
</ul>
<p>The other fields already have usable defaults. You can leave them unchanged for the first group run, or vary
  them to see how each test turns its selected values into a Maze application command.</p>

<h3 id="shared-values">Setting repeated values</h3>
<p>Several tests need the same <strong>Maze Executable Folder</strong>. Start with Folder Parameter, click
  <strong>Browse</strong> and select the Maze application's <code>v3.0.0</code> folder. The selected value appears
  in both the test editor and its row in the overview table:</p>
{{ media.zoomableImage("/assets/images/screenshots/tutorial/running-a-group/configure-one-test-folder.png", "Folder Parameter configured with the Maze v3.0.0 executable folder in the group configuration", "large") }}
<p>Instead of entering the same folder separately for every test, use the value from that table cell. Hover over
  the configured <strong>Maze Executable Folder</strong> value and select
  <strong>Apply this value to all tests</strong>:</p>
{{ media.zoomableImage("/assets/images/screenshots/tutorial/running-a-group/apply-to-all-tests-menu.png", "Apply this value to all tests action shown for the configured Maze Executable Folder table cell", "large") }}
<p>The folder is copied to every test with the same <strong>Maze Executable Folder</strong> field:</p>
{{ media.zoomableImage("/assets/images/screenshots/tutorial/running-a-group/apply-clicked-on-folder.png", "Group configuration after applying the Maze Executable Folder value to all tests with that field", "large") }}
<p>Folder List Parameter remains empty because it declares the separate <strong>Maze Executable Folders</strong>
  list field. Configure that test independently by adding one or more Maze application folders.</p>

<h3 id="updating-the-plan">Updating the plan</h3>
<p>Changed values are shown as unplanned until they are added to the run plan. If we click
  <strong class="text-accent">Update Plan</strong> now, Orcraft validates the whole group and stops because three
  required fields are still empty:</p>
{{ media.zoomableImage("/assets/images/screenshots/tutorial/running-a-group/updating-plan-partially-config.png", "Missing Arguments dialog after trying to update the partially configured Basic Configuration Parameters group plan", "large") }}
<p>The dialog lists <strong>Maze Executable Folders</strong> for Folder List Parameter,
  <strong>Maze Save/Load File</strong> for File Parameter and <strong>Maze Save/Load Files</strong> for File List
  Parameter. No values are committed to the plan, and the existing plan remains unchanged. After we close the
  dialog, Orcraft takes us to the first missing field so we can continue configuring the group.</p>
{{ media.zoomableImage("/assets/images/screenshots/tutorial/running-a-group/clicking-ok-next-missing.png", "Folder List Parameter and its missing Maze Executable Folders field revealed after closing the Missing Arguments dialog", "large") }}
<p>Clicking <strong>OK</strong> selects Folder List Parameter, scrolls the overview table to the missing
  <strong>Maze Executable Folders</strong> column and reveals the field in the editor. Add one or more Maze
  application folders here, then repeat the update attempt to find and configure any remaining missing
  arguments.</p>
<p>After configuring the folder list and the required file fields, every test is valid. The orange diamonds and
  purple values show that these changes are complete but still different from the current plan:</p>
{{ media.zoomableImage("/assets/images/screenshots/tutorial/running-a-group/all-configured-unplanned.png", "Fully configured Basic Configuration Parameters group with unplanned values marked by orange diamonds", "large") }}
<p>Select <strong class="text-accent">Update Plan</strong> again. Validation now passes, so Orcraft asks us to
  confirm that the current configuration should overwrite the existing planned values:</p>
{{ media.zoomableImage("/assets/images/screenshots/tutorial/running-a-group/update-plan-confirmation-dialog.png", "Confirmation dialog asking whether to apply the current group configuration as the new plan", "large") }}
<p>Select <strong>Yes</strong> to update the plan for every test in the group. The values turn blue, the orange
  diamonds disappear and <strong class="text-accent">Update Plan</strong> becomes disabled because the current
  configuration now matches the plan:</p>
{{ media.zoomableImage("/assets/images/screenshots/tutorial/running-a-group/updated-plan.png", "Basic Configuration Parameters group after all current values have been saved to the plan", "large") }}
<p>We could also run the group with unplanned values, just as we did with an individual test, but every required
  field would still need to be complete.</p>

<h2 id="running-the-group">Running the group</h2>
<p>Select <strong>Run</strong> from the group configuration. Orcraft validates every selected test before the run
  begins. If a required value is missing, the Missing Arguments dialog identifies the test and field that still
  need attention; return to that test in the configuration tree, set the value and run again.</p>
<p>Once validation passes, the group runs its child tests in their declared order, from Folder Parameter through
  String Parameter. Each child keeps its own log and result, while the group node shows the aggregate progress
  and final outcome.</p>

<h2 id="reading-the-results">Reading the results</h2>
<p>Expand the completed group run in the execution tree to inspect each test. Select a child result to read its
  command, captured Maze application output and final status. Select the group result for the combined view of
  the run.</p>
<p>A group can finish successfully only when all of its child tests finish successfully. If one fails or errors,
  open that test's result first: its configuration table records the exact parameter values used for that run,
  followed by the command output and failure details.</p>